-- One ask_aar_snapshots row for ASK 591 with its fix 1 and fix 2, and its ask_aar_builders row.
-- READ BY W3 FOR THIS ROW: Wall 11539 to 11544, 11546, 11547, 11554 to 11557, 11559, 11561 in full by SQL; ask591/w4/notes591.md, read591_notes.md, b1/mig591.sql, b1/build591.cjs and fix2/fix2.sql in full; the live table, log and the definition md5 of the seven functions by SQL; md5sum by W3 on every file named.
-- NOT READ BY W3: the cards and the presses in W4's thread; W1's grade and readback files; audit rows 41446, 41463, 41468 (ids taken from the Wall posts); the dashboard files as served.
-- md5_written: adbadc73 (migration), e8a3c37a (engine target), 5142e02e (fix 1 engine target), f29b7095 (fix 1 SQL), 47b637c5 (the live save definition after fix 2; a guarded replacement has no target file). W1 CONFIRMS e8a3c37a AND 47b637c5 WHEN IT GRADES THIS ROW.
BEGIN;
SET LOCAL truth.session_id = '<COORDINATOR SESSION, registered to seat 36>';
WITH s AS (
INSERT INTO ask_aar_snapshots (ask, rev, title, objective, objective_met, objective_met_reason, objective_source, written_by, prior_row, operator_words, card, owner_seat, plan, build_files, revert, grades, md5_written, audit_ids, objects, tests, readbacks, run_evidence, manuals, status, sources)
VALUES (591, '0', $t$ASK 591: the judge order is a table the operator sets from the dashboard (with fix 1 and fix 2)$t$,
  $t$The operator can order the judges and the alternates himself, on a dashboard page, and the engine seats from that order. Before, the order stood as fixed arrays in the engine code (Init Seats ORDER0 and __ALT, Accept Build ORDER), so a change of order needed an engine build. (Plan ask591/w3/plan591.md; the operator asked at 23:23 CST 2026-11-23 and again at 00:41 CST 2026-11-24, and pressed "Build it" at 00:46 CST 2026-11-24, ruling row 517.)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Three writes by W4, each on the operator's press in W4's thread as the Wall and the audit rows give them. (1) ASK 591, press "Write all three", written 08:51 CST 2026-11-24 (Wall 11543; audit 41446). Database (mig591.sql adbadc73): tables odv1_judge_order (seeded from the live order: panel chatgpt, sol, sol62; alternates gemini, spark, qwen4max, argon, sonnet) and odv1_judge_order_log (version 1); functions odv1_judge_order_lists, _fault, _read, _save, dash_judge_order, dash_judge_lineup; three dash_api actions (dash_api 9888582a to a866c092). Engine 489b977b to 347f3e21, 422 to 423 nodes, child untouched: new node Judge Order Read between each start path and Accept Models; Accept Build ORDER, Init Seats ORDER0 and __ALT come from the read; Init Seats' output gains judge_order; Build Save Body adds one review_notes line "[JUDGE ORDER v<n>: ...]"; a missing or bad read stops the run with no fallback order. Dashboard: new tab "Judge order" (judge591.js), patch.js loads it, odv1.js loses haiku from its static list. W1 readback: engine MATCH, database MATCH, dashboard files MATCH (Wall 11544, 11547). (2) Fix 1, press "Write the fix", written 09:21 CST (Wall 11556; audit 41463), after the operator's words of 09:18 CST as Wall 11554 gives them: "i see single judge ... we don't have single judge anymore". Engine 137378eb to 6834c21b: Build Save Body's review line loses "; single judge <seat>". Database: dash_judge_lineup f704ad29 to caea9e6c, no single judge computed or returned. Dashboard: the "Single judge" row deleted (judge591.js sha1 b00c6868). W1 readback MATCH (Wall 11557). (3) Fix 2, press "Write it now", written 09:34 CST (Wall 11559; audit 41468): the operator's Save on the page failed with "requires a WHERE clause" (21000), because odv1_judge_order_save cleared the table with a bare DELETE and the dashboard's database role runs with the safeupdate guard; the save rolled back whole (version stayed 1, 8 rows). One line changed: the clearing ends WHERE true (definition f0dae4d1 to 47b637c5). W1 readback MATCH (Wall 11561). MISTAKES in the record: W4 called the page live before the production alias pointed to the new deployment (W1 found it, Wall 11544 F4; W4 moved the alias, Wall 11546). W4's and W1's tests of the save ran without the safeupdate guard, so neither saw the bare DELETE (Wall 11559, 11561). The first build showed a single judge on the page and in the review line although the single judge is switched off (ruling 402); the operator found it. Fix 2 was written with W1's grade PASS ON READING, TEST NOT RUN, because the approval prompt could not reach the operator and he chose to write. Deviations from the plan, both stated and accepted by W1 (Wall 11540, 11542): the panel list needs at least three seats, not four; the save refuses any seat that is not on the reserve recorder's list, where the plan said to warn. IN PART, because no run has executed since the writes (debate_results last row 21:57 CST 2026-11-23), so no run has read the order from the table. The save from the page is shown: after fix 2 the operator saved at 09:43 CST 2026-11-24 (odv1_judge_order_log row 2, saved_by dashboard; the table now holds panel sol, sol62, spark and alternates chatgpt, qwen4max, gemini, argon, sonnet; read by W3 by SQL and by W1, Wall 11572). Left for ASK 598 (W1's F1, Wall 11555): three single-judge texts in Build Save Body and Init Seats' single_judge field.$t$,
  '11413, 11419, 11543, 11556, 11559',
  current_setting('truth.session_id'), NULL,
  to_jsonb($t$His press "Build it" at 00:46 CST 2026-11-24 in the W3 thread (ruling row 517; Wall 11419). His presses in W4's thread as the Wall gives them: "Write all three" (Wall 11543), "Write the fix" (Wall 11556), "Write it now" (Wall 11559). His words of 09:18 CST 2026-11-24 as Wall 11554 quotes them: "i see single judge ... we don't have single judge anymore". W3 did not see the cards or the presses in W4's thread.$t$::text),
  $j${"answer": "Write all three; Write the fix; Write it now", "source": "Wall 11543, 11556, 11559; audit 41446, 41463, 41468", "thread": "W4", "press_time": "08:51, 09:21 and 09:32 CST 2026-11-24 (14:51, 15:21 and 15:32 UTC as the Wall posts give them)", "question": "not in the record W3 read (the cards are in W4's thread)"}$j$::jsonb,
  'W3',
  $j${"md5": "d84a0dd3", "path": "ask591/w3/plan591.md", "note": "W3's plan rev 4 (W1 PASS on rev 3 Wall 11434; rev 4 follows ASK 593)", "source": "md5sum by W3"}$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"md5": "adbadc73", "path": "ask591/w4/b1/mig591.sql", "note": "the migration, rev 1 (W1 F2 fixed)", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11541, 11542"}, {"md5": "761b21b7", "path": "ask591/w4/b1/build591.cjs", "note": "the engine build script", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11539"}, {"md5": "e8a3c37a", "path": "ask591/w4/b1/target_engine_591.json", "note": "the engine target on the J2 live base 489b977b", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "3f8be5a8", "path": "ask591/w4/write/write591.sh", "note": "the engine write script", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11539"}, {"md5": "1a4c27d1", "path": "ask591/w4/write/fetchback_eng591.json", "note": "the engine fetch-back", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "7a2bbdd7", "path": "ask591/w4/dash/judge591.js", "note": "the page tab as first deployed", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11539"}, {"md5": "e7454625", "path": "ask591/w4/dash/patch.js", "note": "loads judge591.js", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11539"}, {"md5": "4f3935d8", "path": "ask591/w4/dash/odv1.js", "note": "haiku out of the static list", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11539"}, {"md5": "f0e158b7", "path": "ask591/w4/fix1/build_fix1.cjs", "note": "fix 1 engine build script", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11554"}, {"md5": "5142e02e", "path": "ask591/w4/fix1/target_engine_fix1.json", "note": "fix 1 engine target on 137378eb", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11554"}, {"md5": "f29b7095", "path": "ask591/w4/fix1/fix1.sql", "note": "fix 1 database change", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11554"}, {"md5": "1aec0757", "path": "ask591/w4/fix1/judge591.js", "note": "fix 1 page file (sha1 b00c6868)", "source": "md5sum and sha1sum by W3; Wall 11554, 11556"}, {"md5": "270e3824", "path": "ask591/w4/fix1/write_fix1.sh", "note": "fix 1 write script", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11554"}, {"md5": "8ce3a31a", "path": "ask591/w4/fix2/fix2.sql", "note": "fix 2: one guarded replacement in odv1_judge_order_save", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "ac74e890", "path": "ask591/w4/notes591.md", "note": "W4's build notes", "source": "md5sum by W3"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j${"copy": "ASK 591: ask591/w4/write/revert591.sql bbff66e6 and revert_eng591.json 0f71a412, and the dashboard alias back to dpl_F4JdWAFWSHCAodqrBa4MtnkpwDA9. Fix 1: ask591/w4/fix1/revert_eng_fix1.json 9d8b4dff, dash_judge_lineup from mig591.sql, alias back to dpl_GfY2EAHyqufMAeza4eBTW6z6jGhm. Fix 2: the odv1_judge_order_save definition in mig591.sql.", "path": "ask591/w4/write/revert591.sql", "source": "Wall 11543, 11556, 11559; md5sum by W3"}$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS on build rev 1 (rev 0 PASS WITH F1, F2 at Wall 11540; F1 stated and F2 fixed; T3 confirmed 16 of 16): the migration", "wall_id": 11542, "md5_graded": "adbadc73", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 11542 names mig591 adbadc73"}, {"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS on the engine build (t591 ALL PASS 8 on its own fetch of 489b977b; 422 to 423 nodes, only the four named nodes and connections; standing 29/29; pair PASS)", "wall_id": 11540, "md5_graded": "e8a3c37a", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 11540 and 11542; the md5 is md5sum by W3 on ask591/w4/b1/target_engine_591.json; Wall 11544 gives target against live 0 diffs. W1 CONFIRMS the md5 when it grades this row"}, {"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS WITH F1 (a note for ASK 598) on fix 1: the engine target changes only Build Save Body", "wall_id": 11555, "md5_graded": "5142e02e", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 11555; the md5 is in Wall 11554"}, {"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS WITH F1 (a note for ASK 598) on fix 1: the database change (240 pairs equal to live less single_judge)", "wall_id": 11555, "md5_graded": "f29b7095", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 11555; the md5 is in Wall 11554"}, {"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS ON READING, TEST NOT RUN, on fix 2 (the approval prompt timed out at W1's seat); readback MATCH", "wall_id": 11561, "md5_graded": "47b637c5", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 11561 gives the live definition md5 47b637c5 as the mig591 body with the one line replaced. W1 CONFIRMS it when it grades this row"}]$j$::jsonb,
  ARRAY['adbadc73','e8a3c37a','5142e02e','f29b7095','47b637c5'], '[41446, 41463, 41468]'::jsonb,
  $j$[{"kind": "database table", "name": "odv1_judge_order", "before": "did not exist", "after": "8 rows; seeded panel chatgpt, sol, sol62 and alternates gemini, spark, qwen4max, argon, sonnet; after the operator's save of 09:43 CST 2026-11-24: panel sol, sol62, spark and alternates chatgpt, qwen4max, gemini, argon, sonnet (read by W3 by SQL)"}, {"kind": "database table", "name": "odv1_judge_order_log", "before": "did not exist", "after": "row 1 the seed (08:53 CST); row 2 the operator's save from the page (09:43 CST 2026-11-24, saved_by dashboard)"}, {"kind": "database functions", "name": "odv1_judge_order_lists, odv1_judge_order_fault, odv1_judge_order_read, odv1_judge_order_save, dash_judge_order, dash_judge_lineup", "before": "did not exist", "after": "live definition md5 (read by W3 by SQL): lists 2e4b27af, fault a50c7ccd, read 8d7de96d, save 47b637c5 (after fix 2), dash_judge_order cc1f0648, dash_judge_lineup caea9e6c (after fix 1)"}, {"kind": "database function", "name": "dash_api", "before": "9888582a", "after": "a866c092: three actions added (judge_order, judge_order_save, judge_lineup)"}, {"kind": "engine workflow", "name": "ODV1 engine", "before": "489b977b, 422 nodes", "after": "347f3e21, 423 nodes (ASK 591); then 6834c21b on base 137378eb (fix 1; ASK 586 J3 was written between). Nodes: Judge Order Read (new), Accept Build, Init Seats, Build Save Body. Child untouched in both writes"}, {"kind": "dashboard deployment", "name": "truth-app-dashboard (production alias truth-app-dashboard.vercel.app)", "before": "dpl_F4JdWAFWSHCAodqrBa4MtnkpwDA9", "after": "dpl_GfY2EAHyqufMAeza4eBTW6z6jGhm (ASK 591; alias moved 09:03 CST), then dpl_AJ7NzE2AUALvibHUT83ez7WgPomX (fix 1)"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"name": "t591.cjs 62af78eb", "result": "ALL PASS 8 on both bases, and at the write: the seeded order equals the live Init Seats output in 360 cases; the read stands before every HTTP call; a missing or bad read stops Accept Build and Init Seats; only the four named nodes change", "source": "notes591.md; Wall 11539, 11540, 11543"}, {"name": "T2.sql 88966caf (dash_judge_lineup against the JS line-ups)", "result": "1800 of 1800 equal. Fault found and fixed before the write: a NULL in the both-Claude test seated sonnet against a Claude debater when the other debater was mimo (32 cases)", "source": "notes591.md; Wall 11539"}, {"name": "T3 ee2ced0c (the save's refusals, temporary tables)", "result": "16 of 16 meaningful cases PASS; case 9 was a bad case and proved nothing (W4's stated mistake). It ran without the safeupdate guard and so could not see the fault fix 2 mends", "source": "Wall 11541, 11542, 11559"}, {"name": "standing set and pair", "result": "29/29 and PASS at each engine write", "source": "Wall 11543, 11556"}, {"name": "test_fix1.sql 7c4a4442", "result": "240 debater pairs: 240 equal to live less single_judge, 0 carry single_judge, 0 errors (W4, and W1's own run)", "source": "Wall 11554, 11555"}, {"name": "test_fix2.sql 7039f022", "result": "NOT RUN: the approval prompt timed out. The proof came from use: the operator's save of 09:43 CST 2026-11-24 succeeded (log row 2), read back by W1 (Wall 11572)", "source": "Wall 11559, 11561"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"seat": "W1", "wall_id": 11547, "result": "ASK 591: engine, database and dashboard MATCH (Wall 11544 gave engine MATCH, database MATCH with F3 on grants, and F4: the production alias still pointed to the old deployment; F4 fixed by W4 at 09:03 CST, F3 stated and accepted)"}, {"seat": "W1", "wall_id": 11557, "result": "fix 1: MATCH (engine 6834c21b, only Build Save Body against 137378eb; dash_judge_lineup caea9e6c; alias on dpl_AJ7N, judge591.js sha1 b00c6868)"}, {"seat": "W1", "wall_id": 11561, "result": "fix 2: MATCH (save definition 47b637c5; table still 8 rows, version 1)"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j${"case": "THE SAVE IS SHOWN: log row 2 at 09:43 CST 2026-11-24. THE ENGINE READ IS UNEXERCISED: no run since the writes. EXPECT on the first run: one execution of Judge Order Read before Accept Models; Init Seats' output carries judge_order with the version of the table; review_notes holds one line \"[JUDGE ORDER v<n>: panel list ...; alternates list ... | SEATED: panel ...; reserve ...; alternates ...]\" with no single judge named; the seated panel is the one the table's order gives for the pair. With the order as saved at 09:43 CST the line reads v2.", "source": "Wall 11543, 11556, 11559, 11561, 11572; the pre-run sheet aar/w3/prerun_objectives_1124.md 0cc2e269; the EXPECT is W3's reading"}$j$::jsonb,
